---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import Method from '../components/Method.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Pranjal Pandey | Practical AI Strategy for Founders & Leaders"
  description="Practical AI strategy for founders and leaders. I help companies turn AI pilots into real workflows. Founder at 19, PhD researcher in multi-agent systems at IIT Jodhpur." home>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical AI strategy for founders & leaders</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">AI strategy that survives <span>Monday morning.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">I help founders and leadership teams work out where AI actually fits, and turn AI pilots into workflows their teams use every day.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/guide/">Get the free guide <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/call/">Book a call <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Portrait hero />
    </section>
    <div class="credentials" aria-label="Background">
      <span>Building software <strong>since 2013</strong>. Founder <strong>at 19</strong>.</span>
      <span>Founder, <strong>Taskflo AI</strong></span>
      <span>PhD researcher, <strong>IIT Jodhpur</strong></span>
    </div>
    <section class="section blockers">
      <div><h2>Everyone has an AI strategy deck. Few have AI that works.</h2></div>
      <dl class="blocker-list">
        <div><span class="number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><dt>Too many ideas. No clear priority.</dt><dd>Twenty possible use cases, but no shared answer to which one matters first.</dd></div></div>
        <div><span class="number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><dt>Permissions are an afterthought.</dt><dd>Nobody can say where the data goes or what the AI is allowed to touch.</dd></div></div>
        <div><span class="number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><dt>The pilot never becomes a habit.</dt><dd>It worked in the demo. It didn't fit the people and process doing the work.</dd></div></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section class="section method-section" id="method">
      <div class="section-intro"><div><h2>Diagnose. Decide. Build.</h2></div><p>Find the blocker, choose the trade-off, then build something your team can own. The output is a useful next move, not a giant report.</p></div>
      <Method />
      <div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/work/">See how we can work together <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section proof-grid">
      <div class="proof-intro"><h2>One question.<br />Different scales.</h2><p>What does it take for a system to stay useful? I've followed that question from my first software at 15 to enterprise workflows and multi-agent research.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">The longer story <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></div>
      <div class="ledger">
        <article class="ledger-entry"><span class="mono">01 / Building</span><h3>Taskflo AI</h3><p>A platform that lets companies run AI agent workflows inside their own cloud, with every action checked and logged. Built for teams whose security people ask good questions.</p><a class="text-link" href={site.taskflo}>Explore Taskflo AI <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
        <article class="ledger-entry"><span class="mono">02 / Applied work</span><h3>From architecture to the workflow.</h3><p>Enterprise platforms, AI integrations and the practical decisions around permissions, ownership and delivery.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/">What that looks like in an engagement <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
        <article class="ledger-entry"><span class="mono">03 / Research</span><h3>How should agents divide the work?</h3><p>PhD research at IIT Jodhpur in multi-agent systems, fair division and allocation. Expected completion: 2028.</p><a class="text-link" href="/research/">Explore the research <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section guide-section" id="guide">
      <div class="guide-title-card" aria-label="AI Strategy Starter guide">
        <span class="mono">A practical starting point / Free guide</span>
        <h3>AI Strategy Starter</h3>
        <div><div class="guide-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><p>For Founders & Leaders</p><p class="fine-print">Pranjal Pandey</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Start with the right questions</p><h2>Before you build another pilot.</h2><p class="muted">A short, practical guide to working out where AI fits in your business.</p>
        <ul class="guide-contents"><li>Five questions to ask before an AI project.</li><li>How to choose your first three workflows.</li><li>The mistakes that stop a pilot becoming useful.</li></ul>
        <Signup id="home-email" />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-intro"><div><h2>A company decision.<br />Or your own next move.</h2></div><p>Different starting points, different kinds of work. The free company call is for fit; paid sessions are for focused planning.</p></div>
      <div class="offer-list">
        <article class="offer-row"><span class="mono">For companies</span><div><h3>Unstick your AI pilot.</h3><p>I help you pick the AI work that matters, get it past security, and take it to production. Free intro call, workflow audit, build, then ongoing advisory.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/work/">Work with me <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
        <article class="offer-row"><span class="mono">For individuals</span><div><h3>Work through your AI strategy question.</h3><p>Start with the free guide, or book a focused 90-minute strategy session or a separate 60-minute career and portfolio session.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/work/#sessions">Explore sessions <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section writing-preview">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Practical AI</p><h2>From the monthly letter.</h2><p>Practical AI strategy for founders and leaders: what works, what stalls, and how to make AI stick. One long letter a month, no fluff.</p><a class="text-link" href="/writing/">Writing & the monthly letter <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></div>
      <div class="empty-note"><span class="mono">The archive starts here.</span><p>No essays published here yet. In the meantime, my public research is available to read, and I share updates on LinkedIn.</p><a class="text-link" href={site.linkedin}>Find me on LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section close"><h2>Got an AI idea that's stuck?</h2><p>If you're trying to work out where AI fits in your team or your company, I'm always happy to talk. No pitch deck needed.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/call/">Book a call <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Or email me</a></div></section>
  </div>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/home';
  </script>
</Layout>
